WEBVTT

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:06.510
<i>And now an update on the vicious 
assault that occurred yesterday</i>

00:00:06.510 --> 00:00:07.980
<i>in front of Toyosu station.</i>

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:10.180
<i>The suspect continues 
to deny involvement,</i>

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:11.500
<i>saying she has no recollection 
of the incident.</i>

00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:15.760
<i>Suspects of the two assaults occurring 
near Tachikawa earlier this month</i>

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:15.050
Hey, Pai-Pai, all this...

00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:17.530
is by the bad Gatchaman, right?

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:18.360
<i>have also denied involvement, 
citing similar reasons.</i>

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:19.570
We don't know that.

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:20.540
<i>Criminal psychologists 
have speculated that</i>

00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:20.810
Stop calling me Pai-Pai.

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:22.250
<i>the series of incidents 
may have been triggered</i>

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:24.460
That's what it meant by 
"It's all your fault."

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:24.390
<i>by people's everyday stresses 
that subconsciously erupted...</i>

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:26.100
Okay. Question!

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:27.840
If this bad Gatchaman does

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.640
even worse stuff, 
what are we going to do?

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:34.560
Well, um...

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:38.170
Of course, we'd all 
deal with it together!

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:39.840
Really?

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:43.880
Wouldn't Pai-Pai just run away 
when the time comes?

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:45.990
O-Of course not!

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:49.100
I'm your leader!

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:53.040
We Gatchaman have a duty 
to protect this planet!

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:54.750
Anyway, stop calling me Pai-Pai!

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:55.870
Question!

00:00:55.870 --> 00:00:59.430
Have Gatchaman ever fought together?

00:00:59.430 --> 00:01:00.380
That has...

00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:01.040
No!

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:02.380
Question!

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:05.020
You sure like questions.

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:08.170
Why do Gatchaman sneak around?

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:11.770
Shouldn't we act more like

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:13.610
the police or the self-defense force?

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:14.270
What?

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:15.510
Well...

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:17.680
Maybe you have a point...

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:19.800
We can't.

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:21.700
Why?

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:24.290
Because... those are the rules.

00:01:24.290 --> 00:01:26.810
What?! Who made those rules?

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:28.780
What do they mean, Senpai?

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:30.780
What? Well...

00:01:31.270 --> 00:01:33.190
If I could act more openly...

00:01:33.190 --> 00:01:33.910
Sugane!

00:01:33.910 --> 00:01:34.460
Uh, yes?

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:35.170
Newbie!

00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:36.410
I'm Hajime!

00:01:37.510 --> 00:01:39.100
Listen, you two!

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:45.040
We Gatchaman have special powers 
normal humans do not have.

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:49.580
We must never let those powers 
fall into their hands!

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:52.860
We're not sneaking around.

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:55.050
We're solving problems 
without causing the human race

00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:57.240
unnecessary concern or worry.

00:01:57.620 --> 00:02:01.430
Then why is the bad Gatchaman 
doing as it pleases?

00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:02.780
Because it is bad!

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:05.220
Because there are those who use 
the power for ill, we must strive,

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:08.440
all the more, to be careful about 
how we use our own abilities!

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:12.530
But what if there's an emergency 
that won't let us do that?

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:17.610
What if the world goes 
up in a big, red blaze?

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:20.530
Then the human race 
will be super worried.

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:22.360
I don't get it.

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:26.530
That'd make people say 
GALAX is doing more.

00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:27.790
That's going too far.

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:27.870
Oh, Hajime-chan. 
Hi, D-san!

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:29.080
Oh, Hajime-chan. 
Aw, your hair's different. Way too cute! 
Hi, D-san!

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:31.150
Don't put us Gatchaman 
on the same level as GALAX!

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:30.690
Oh, Hajime-chan. 
Aw, your hair's different. Way too cute! 
Hi, D-san! Hee Hee. Oh.

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:32.170
Can you tell me where Utsutsu-chan's room is?

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:33.000
Oh? You got a smart phone.

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:32.990
Can you tell me where Utsutsu-chan's room is? 
Okay. Come with me.

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:35.700
You're using GALAX!

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:37.850
No! This is research!

00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:41.430
Senpai, come join 
the collage community!

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:43.020
No way I'd join that!

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:46.700
Oh, a message from JJ.

00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:51.910
When a large box has 
vanished into darkness,

00:02:51.910 --> 00:02:56.570
the broken child 
will finally reveal itself to us.

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:58.900
The white bird shall bear witness.

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:00.870
The broken child?

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:02.500
It's <i>it</i>!

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:04.490
It will finally appear... 
before... us...

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:07.370
Leader!

00:03:08.890 --> 00:03:11.330
The white bird... Huh...

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:36.880
Rui, what is the matter?

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:40.300
You have not moved for two hours.

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:44.720
X, I'll tell you what 
I'm really thinking.

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:50.220
You're the only one I can trust, X.

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:51.810
Thank you.

00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:54.770
That is probably what 
I should say in response.

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:58.730
You're interesting, X.

00:04:58.730 --> 00:05:00.320
You're just like a person.

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:07.070
Rui, your decision appears 
to have caused some confusion.

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:10.080
Is it true that LOAD runs GALAX?

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:11.200
Apparently.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:13.580
He sure looks suspicious, doesn't he?

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:16.420
Isn't it run by X?

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:20.000
You mean that goth-lolita four-eyes 
is the one who picked us?

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.400
What's this...

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:22.760
So creepy.

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:23.670
"SDWORC"?

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:26.380
I mean, he's totally 
ordering us around.

00:05:24.470 --> 00:05:26.380
Please read it backwards.

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:28.970
CROWDS, huh...

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:34.770
It is a community created today 
by a subset of the Hundred.

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:36.520
I closed it down immediately,

00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:40.110
but there will be trouble 
if this becomes widespread.

00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:43.280
My decision is final, no matter what.

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:45.820
The use of CROWDS is forbidden 
for the time being.

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:48.240
Shall I force them 
to withdraw from the Hundred?

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:50.120
Who is their representative?

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:52.200
Number 26.

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:55.580
I remember.

00:05:56.210 --> 00:05:58.580
He's always wanted to use CROWDS.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:00.420
Call him up.

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:01.920
Understood.

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:05.260
I will relay your opinion to Number 26.

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:07.970
No, I will speak with him directly.

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:09.390
Understood.

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:13.430
Morning, Number 26.

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:16.770
I have a name: Umeda.

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:19.560
Morning, Umeda-san.

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:21.700
This is LOAD, right?

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:23.270
Yes.

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:25.360
What's your real name?

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:29.280
I'm sorry, but my policy is not to say.

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:30.530
Why?

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:35.700
Because I believe GALAX 
 doesn't need a solitary leader.

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:38.460
No, it's because you want to be able

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:41.240
to abandon everything and be 
irresponsible when the time comes.

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:43.880
It does not matter 
what you think of it.

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:47.380
It appears you are dissatisfied with me.

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:48.840
You must know why.

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:51.470
The use of CROWDS 
is forbidden for the time being.

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:53.050
Explain why.

00:06:53.350 --> 00:06:56.770
It has developed minor 
functionality issues.

00:06:57.560 --> 00:06:59.690
You're a bad liar.

00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:01.230
What do you mean?

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:03.810
You want to get all the 
credit, don't you?

00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:04.980
Credit?

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:06.780
Don't play dumb.

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:10.150
If used, CROWDS can 
easily change the world.

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:11.700
For example?

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:16.850
For example, we can just 
kill incompetent politicians.

00:07:17.290 --> 00:07:19.580
Execute vile criminals.

00:07:20.060 --> 00:07:23.210
Crush corporations
that are repeat offenders.

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:26.170
Would that change the world?

00:07:26.170 --> 00:07:28.510
Isn't that what CROWDS is for?

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:32.890
Will the world change, 
just by saving people's lives?

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:35.640
This is the real deal.

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:38.680
But now you want 
to keep CROWDS for yourself,

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:41.020
to give yourself credit.

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:44.020
What is this "credit" you speak of?

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:46.320
What is it that you want?

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:49.570
Don't put on airs, LOAD.

00:07:49.570 --> 00:07:51.530
Let's get real.

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:55.660
We, the Hundred, have endangered

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:57.910
ourselves many times 
over for this world.

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:01.330
Isn't it about time that 
our efforts are rewarded?

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:04.520
The world is full of praise 
for what we've done.

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:07.040
It's about time we revealed ourselves.

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:09.510
Everyone can become heroes.

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:12.260
And that's "credit"?

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:15.550
You want praise?

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:17.760
Reputation?

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:21.280
Not just me. Everyone thinks the same.

00:08:21.730 --> 00:08:22.850
Is that true?

00:08:23.350 --> 00:08:26.320
I am interested in becoming 
neither a hero nor a leader.

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:31.240
A world that lionizes heroes 
and leaders is still primitive.

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:33.400
Until individuals who are neither

00:08:34.070 --> 00:08:37.370
change their way of thinking 
and rise to action,

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:41.250
the world can never be updated.

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:44.420
Like I said, ditch the idealism!

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:47.250
Our way of thinking 
had changed way before!

00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:49.090
This is a revolution, right?

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:54.430
The world will never change if 
revolutionaries just sneak around!

00:08:54.930 --> 00:08:56.720
Everyone's raring to go!

00:08:56.720 --> 00:08:58.680
Let us use CROWDS already!

00:08:59.050 --> 00:09:02.980
Umeda-san, are you having 
any fun right now?

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:04.060
Huh?

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:07.440
Do you feel any joy 
in being one of the Hundred?

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:10.320
I have no clue what you're getting at.

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:12.440
I do feel joy.

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:15.150
It's a joy that comes 
from deep within.

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:18.870
It's not based on external factors like

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:20.780
money, reputation, status, or reward.

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:24.120
It stems from connecting with 
people possessing a similar purpose,

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:26.250
giving a helping hand to those in need,

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:30.340
then working together to right wrongs.

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:33.670
It is a joy that comes from 
within, innate to mankind.

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:36.680
The circle of community will 
spread, eventually creating

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:39.260
a world where everyone will help 
each other without compensation.

00:09:40.050 --> 00:09:43.060
It will be a world 
without heroes and leaders,

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:45.980
where everyone is equal, 
working side by side,

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:48.690
slowly changing the world without

00:09:48.690 --> 00:09:50.690
holding their own 
deeds in high esteem.

00:09:51.230 --> 00:09:53.400
That is the revolution GALAX aims for.

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:59.370
As if anyone would be satisfied 
by a scam like that.

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:00.570
A scam?

00:10:00.570 --> 00:10:01.830
Yeah, that's right.

00:10:01.830 --> 00:10:04.080
LOAD, you don't have the backbone.

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:08.460
You think we'll be satisfied 
with wishy-washy logic like that?

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:11.420
But I believed you.

00:10:11.420 --> 00:10:13.880
Your cheer, optimism, 
willingness to help others...

00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:20.010
Your selfless actions both within 
GALAX and without in the real world.

00:10:21.010 --> 00:10:25.020
I felt I could give you special powers

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:27.560
without them being misused.

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:32.060
I believed you would use 
them to update the world.

00:10:33.110 --> 00:10:34.110
Get credit?

00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:35.030
Become heroes?

00:10:35.780 --> 00:10:40.070
I didn't create GALAX 
for such insignificant things!

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:43.870
C'mon, gimme a break.

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:47.000
Please remember, Umeda-san.

00:10:47.660 --> 00:10:52.460
Remember when you first 
reached out and helped a stranger.

00:10:53.790 --> 00:10:55.210
Everything will be all right.

00:10:55.210 --> 00:10:57.010
The world will soon change.

00:10:57.880 --> 00:11:00.630
We will change 
the prevailing sentiment that

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:02.590
money and reputation are everything.

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:08.600
Everyone will soon realize 
the true joy... the true connection.

00:11:09.140 --> 00:11:14.400
They <i>will</i> realize that those 
are things people really desire!

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:15.980
Umeda-san!

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:18.440
Let's change the world together!

00:11:20.650 --> 00:11:22.070
I get it.

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:25.240
Thank you.

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:28.040
I'm glad you understand.

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:29.410
Don't get me wrong.

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:35.290
I really get it that you're 
the one who's a useless leader.

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:41.800
Papa?

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:42.840
Mana.

00:11:44.140 --> 00:11:45.760
What's the matter, Papa?

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:48.520
It's nothing.

00:11:49.270 --> 00:11:50.140
Let's go, yeah?

00:11:51.270 --> 00:11:52.020
Okay.

00:11:55.650 --> 00:12:00.120
X, please withdraw him 
and his friends immediately.

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:01.820
Understood.

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:04.320
The world is regressing...

00:12:05.070 --> 00:12:08.540
It appears I have made a mistake 
in my selection of partners.

00:12:09.240 --> 00:12:12.540
But you have me!

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:19.880
Hey, Rui-Rui.

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:23.510
Why won't you use <i>my</i> power?

00:12:23.510 --> 00:12:25.640
Tell me plz!

00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:28.850
Watch where you're going!

00:12:29.430 --> 00:12:30.720
He's a total asshole.

00:12:31.270 --> 00:12:33.270
Rui-san, want me to get him?

00:12:33.270 --> 00:12:34.980
Shut up! Be quiet!

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:40.990
Okay, here's a comment from General X.

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:45.240
Rui, a magnitude 8.5 earthquake

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:48.160
has just occurred in the Kantou region.

00:12:48.660 --> 00:12:51.290
Tens of thousands 
of casualties are expected from

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:54.040
a massive tsunami 
and collapsed buildings.

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:56.710
The power of CROWDS is needed.

00:12:56.710 --> 00:12:57.920
Stop it!

00:12:59.420 --> 00:13:02.010
The power of CROWDS is needed.

00:13:02.010 --> 00:13:03.010
Stop!

00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:06.550
The power of CROWDS is needed.

00:13:07.510 --> 00:13:10.510
Stop!

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:16.150
Oh, it's not shaking?

00:13:16.690 --> 00:13:18.560
It's got to be shaking.

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:21.940
The world's shaking up a storm.

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:23.440
Shaking!

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:52.930
GALAX Collage Offline
Meeting in Fukushima

00:13:55.180 --> 00:13:56.230
How about this ribbon?

00:13:56.640 --> 00:13:57.600
How's that?

00:13:59.690 --> 00:14:00.520
Huh?

00:14:00.520 --> 00:14:02.110
There's no communications network?

00:14:02.730 --> 00:14:04.860
Now that you mention it, no.

00:14:05.070 --> 00:14:08.320
But the police and the self-defense force 
are right across from each other, right?

00:14:08.320 --> 00:14:10.820
The fire station and 
the city hall are nearby, too.

00:14:10.820 --> 00:14:12.950
What would you do if anything 
happened to Tachikawa?

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:15.950
I can't believe what she's talking 
about with people like them.

00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:22.210
"The broken child will reveal itself." 
What's that supposed to mean?

00:14:22.630 --> 00:14:23.920
What else?

00:14:23.920 --> 00:14:26.590
It's talking about the crazy Gatchaman.

00:14:26.590 --> 00:14:29.300
Wow! Jou-san, you're so good!

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:32.350
You've got good taste! 
You're a cool customer, too.

00:14:32.350 --> 00:14:33.470
Isn't he?

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:34.640
He's great!

00:14:33.810 --> 00:14:36.270
Jou-san, we didn't 
come here to have fun.

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:37.980
I know.

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:40.060
"The white bird shall bear witness."

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:42.940
Don't take your eyes off that girl.

00:14:44.840 --> 00:14:46.530
What's this stick?

00:14:48.110 --> 00:14:50.110
I-It's nothing!

00:14:50.450 --> 00:14:52.740
Wait! A sword, maybe?

00:14:52.740 --> 00:14:54.660
You've got no taste!

00:14:54.660 --> 00:14:56.700
Wait! Please stop!

00:14:56.700 --> 00:14:57.750
Jou-san!

00:15:00.750 --> 00:15:02.790
That's totally weird.

00:15:03.170 --> 00:15:05.170
Everyone's connected on GALAX,

00:15:05.170 --> 00:15:07.320
but not in the real world?

00:15:07.670 --> 00:15:09.340
That's true.

00:15:09.340 --> 00:15:12.800
Well, we've gone out 
a couple of times for drinks.

00:15:13.180 --> 00:15:16.890
Well, why don't we exchange 
numbers while we're at it?

00:15:16.890 --> 00:15:19.640
Isn't this great? It's the F-15.

00:15:19.640 --> 00:15:23.270
This tail wing part was 
super hard to get right.

00:15:23.270 --> 00:15:26.360
It's not about whether it's hard to do.

00:15:26.360 --> 00:15:28.400
We're going to teach children,

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:29.900
so we should choose 
something more positive—

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:31.450
You're acting all feminine,

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:34.070
but you totally shoot guns 
when you have to, right?

00:15:34.070 --> 00:15:36.040
Must be nice being a cop 
to do as you please.

00:15:36.040 --> 00:15:38.940
There you go again, 
bringing up work at the drop of a hat.

00:15:39.410 --> 00:15:40.790
I feel sorry for your husband!

00:15:40.790 --> 00:15:42.290
What's my husband got to do with it?

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:44.670
I mean, it's better than being single.

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:46.630
What'd you say?!

00:15:46.740 --> 00:15:47.800
What?

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:49.880
Now, now. It'll be fine.

00:15:49.880 --> 00:15:52.630
When it counts, we come together.

00:15:55.380 --> 00:15:58.390
Okay, Tachikawa team! 
Be nice to each other!

00:15:58.390 --> 00:16:00.520
Let's all go out for drinks again!

00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:01.890
That sounds like a great idea.

00:16:10.070 --> 00:16:12.240
Oh, here it comes!

00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:14.570
Into the tunnel we go!

00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:17.410
"When a large box..."

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:19.240
"Has vanished into darkness"!

00:16:28.170 --> 00:16:29.550
Good god!

00:16:32.590 --> 00:16:35.510
Hey, the tunnel's collapsed!

00:16:42.390 --> 00:16:44.560
Are you okay!?

00:16:44.560 --> 00:16:45.400
Hey!

00:16:46.980 --> 00:16:48.610
Requesting immediate assistance!

00:16:48.610 --> 00:16:49.400
The location is, um...

00:16:49.400 --> 00:16:51.650
Joufuku Expressway, 
before Kamishiro Pass.

00:16:52.030 --> 00:16:54.410
One of the tunnel's 
ceiling panels has collapsed.

00:16:54.410 --> 00:16:56.120
More than twenty vehicles and

00:16:56.120 --> 00:16:59.240
approximately sixty people 
are trapped in the debris.

00:16:59.790 --> 00:17:02.120
Their rescue is a priority,

00:17:02.120 --> 00:17:03.870
but there is a risk of fire.

00:17:03.870 --> 00:17:05.870
Please move with caution.

00:17:06.380 --> 00:17:10.500
Please evacuate children and the 
elderly from the accident site first.

00:17:11.590 --> 00:17:13.970
Please take advantage 
of your skills as a nurse.

00:17:14.220 --> 00:17:16.930
Your skills are needed right now.

00:17:20.060 --> 00:17:21.470
All right!

00:17:20.810 --> 00:17:21.470
Okay!

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:22.770
Are you all right?

00:17:22.770 --> 00:17:23.810
Can you walk?

00:17:24.440 --> 00:17:27.270
Excuse me! Please carry him to safety.

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:33.280
There are not enough people on-site.

00:17:33.280 --> 00:17:34.940
CROWDS is needed.

00:17:37.450 --> 00:17:38.910
What is the matter, Rui?

00:17:39.580 --> 00:17:41.490
We're not using CROWDS anymore.

00:17:41.490 --> 00:17:42.700
That's what I decided, right?

00:17:42.910 --> 00:17:46.830
However, if we do not hurry, 
many lives will be lost.

00:17:46.830 --> 00:17:50.500
Without intervention, 
dozens of casualties are projected.

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:51.880
I know!

00:17:51.880 --> 00:17:54.350
I know that...

00:17:55.510 --> 00:17:58.720
CROWDS is not that alien's power.

00:17:58.740 --> 00:18:03.060
<b>I can't stand it anymore. 
We can't let young'uns die.
At this rate, there will be a secondary disaster.</b>

00:18:00.140 --> 00:18:04.480
CROWDS is your power, Rui.

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:05.770
<b>Save as many people as possible! 
 Is there a reason? 
I can't go! Please help.</b>

00:18:08.350 --> 00:18:10.170
Someone, help!

00:18:09.690 --> 00:18:12.860
Please, I need guys here to help!

00:18:13.030 --> 00:18:14.280
Please!

00:18:19.030 --> 00:18:20.160
Thank you.

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:21.700
Utsutsu-chan!

00:18:29.170 --> 00:18:30.830
Okay, go!

00:18:34.380 --> 00:18:35.550
Where are the firefighters?

00:18:35.550 --> 00:18:37.170
They'll be here in twenty minutes.

00:18:37.170 --> 00:18:39.130
A self-defense force 
helicopter is on its way.

00:18:39.130 --> 00:18:40.050
Let's hurry!

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:42.600
If the remaining ceiling panels 
collapse, we're done for!

00:18:42.970 --> 00:18:44.810
If a fire starts...

00:18:46.310 --> 00:18:48.850
Then we'll just have to run.

00:18:48.850 --> 00:18:50.570
We're going to abandon them?!

00:18:50.560 --> 00:18:52.770
We're hurrying, 
so we don't have to do that.

00:18:52.770 --> 00:18:54.470
Calm down, both of you.

00:18:55.620 --> 00:18:57.370
How many cars are left?

00:18:57.370 --> 00:19:01.530
There are five more trapped 
upwards from where you are.

00:19:02.210 --> 00:19:04.150
Still so many...

00:19:05.060 --> 00:19:07.080
Will you help us?

00:19:07.650 --> 00:19:10.620
Of course. I'm a cop.

00:19:12.720 --> 00:19:14.440
Okay, let's go!

00:19:18.780 --> 00:19:19.550
Look out!

00:19:36.560 --> 00:19:37.740
What?

00:19:37.740 --> 00:19:39.300
What's that?

00:19:39.300 --> 00:19:40.200
Amnesia...

00:19:44.640 --> 00:19:46.140
The Effect is already active.

00:19:46.140 --> 00:19:47.390
What's that?

00:19:47.390 --> 00:19:49.070
By whom?

00:19:47.390 --> 00:19:49.960
What's going on?

00:19:49.750 --> 00:19:51.450
It can't be... Is that the one?

00:19:52.670 --> 00:19:54.130
"The broken child"!

00:19:54.430 --> 00:19:57.230
Let's go. There can be no casualties.

00:19:58.640 --> 00:20:00.170
Play the Game...

00:20:04.760 --> 00:20:06.970
First, speak to passengers 
to see if they are conscious,

00:20:06.970 --> 00:20:08.800
and check if their airways 
are obstructed or not.

00:20:09.140 --> 00:20:11.210
If they need CPR, bring them here.

00:20:11.600 --> 00:20:12.810
Don't worry.

00:20:12.810 --> 00:20:14.890
We <i>will</i> save all of them without fail.

00:20:17.480 --> 00:20:19.780
It'll be okay.
I hope everyone makes it...

00:20:20.030 --> 00:20:22.750
Looks like things are 
going to be okay here.

00:20:24.560 --> 00:20:26.190
Wow!

00:20:26.190 --> 00:20:27.590
Who are they?

00:20:26.190 --> 00:20:29.580
We have to do our part, too!

00:20:29.800 --> 00:20:30.770
Newbie.

00:20:30.770 --> 00:20:31.910
I'm Hajime.

00:20:31.910 --> 00:20:33.550
Don't use your Gatchaman powers.

00:20:33.930 --> 00:20:35.540
Boo.

00:20:34.470 --> 00:20:35.540
You either, Utsutsu.

00:20:37.050 --> 00:20:39.590
Get out of the tunnel!

00:20:39.800 --> 00:20:41.530
Hurry!

00:20:55.600 --> 00:20:57.520
Hey, Newbie!

00:20:57.520 --> 00:20:59.140
Gatcha—

00:20:59.670 --> 00:21:01.360
What are you thinking?!

00:21:01.810 --> 00:21:05.560
Senpai, aren't there times 
when you find yourself taking

00:21:05.560 --> 00:21:07.090
action without even thinking about it?

00:21:07.530 --> 00:21:09.980
What are you talking about?

00:21:09.980 --> 00:21:10.940
Hey!

00:21:11.280 --> 00:21:12.880
The time is now!

00:21:13.520 --> 00:21:15.490
That's what heroes do!

00:21:15.490 --> 00:21:17.710
Amnesia Effect!

00:21:17.710 --> 00:21:19.930
Wait!

00:21:19.000 --> 00:21:22.280
Go, Bird!

00:21:28.250 --> 00:21:32.390
Are you okay!?

00:21:41.420 --> 00:21:42.670
It can't be...
